Package: binwise
Type: Package
Title: Diagnose and Compare Binning Choices
Version: 0.0.17
Authors@R: person("Keith A.", "Preble", email = "preblek25@ecu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Diagnose numeric variables before categorization. Summarize missing
    values, exact zeros, percentiles, and candidate bin counts. Preserve ties,
    identify sparse bins, and optionally treat zero as its own category.
    Compare quantile, equal-width, and custom schemes with plain-language
    assessments and plots. Apply saved boundaries to create categorical
    variables and explore reproducible simulated examples. Compare continuous
    and binned predictors in linear and binary logistic models, with optional
    two-variable interactions, common samples, predictions, pointwise confidence
    intervals, bin support counts, and plain-language model assessments.
    Validate prediction workflows with shared grouped folds, training-only
    bin recipes, paired loss comparisons, and optional clustered score intervals.
    Include natural cubic spline comparators with training-only knots to evaluate
    categorization against flexible continuous relationships.
LazyData: true
